Here are concrete, security-focused suggestions for improving error handling and input validation in `app.js`, adapted to a small Express app like this.

### 1. Add a centralized error handler

Right now, if anything throws inside a route, Express will send a default error page (possibly with stack traces in development). It’s better to:

- Ensure all errors go through a centralized handler.
- Avoid leaking stack traces or internal details to clients.
- Return consistent JSON error responses.

```js
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

// Basic middleware to parse JSON if you later add POST/PUT routes
app.use(express.json());

// Health check
app.get('/health', (req, res) => {
  try {
    res.json({ status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() });
  } catch (err) {
    // Pass unexpected errors to the centralized handler
    return next(err);
  }
});

// Users endpoint
app.get('/users', (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const users = [
      { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
      { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
    ];
    res.json(users);
  } catch (err) {
    return next(err);
  }
});

// Centralized error handler (must come after routes)
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log full error on the server
  console.error(err);

  // Avoid leaking stack traces to the client
  const status = err.status || 500;
  const message =
    status === 500
      ? 'Internal server error'
      : err.message || 'Unexpected error';

  res.status(status).json({
    error: message,
  });
});

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
});

module.exports = app;
```

Key security aspects:
- Clients never see stack traces or internal error details.
- You can later enrich the error handler with correlation IDs, rate limiting responses, etc.

### 2. Add input validation scaffolding (even if there’s no input yet)

You don’t currently accept inputs (query/body/params), but in practice this file will grow. To prevent future insecure patterns:

